# Force LF for the force-tracked planning roadmap. gsd-sdk roadmap writes were
# landing CRLF in the committed blob (core.autocrlf=true did not prevent it),
# producing whole-file line-ending churn on every 3-line logical update
# (Phase 13 post-review remediation). eol=lf makes the stored blob LF regardless
# of the writer or platform.
.planning/ROADMAP.md text eol=lf

# Vendored minified bundle — treat as binary so autocrlf never rewrites its line
# endings and git shows no diff noise on the third-party file.
docs/vision/chart.umd.min.js binary

# Bundled design-reference artifact (Claude-designed console mockup, encoded blocks) —
# treat as binary: it's a generated reference we don't diff, keep it byte-exact.
docs/vision/console-mockup/tenantless-console.mockup.html binary

# The bundled synthetic `demo` profile is byte-fingerprinted
# (tests/demo_profile.sha256, asserted by tests/test_demo_profile.py) and its
# derivation is byte-reproducible in the pinned canonical builder. Pin its
# checkout to LF so the recorded sha256 is stable on EVERY platform — without
# this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites it to CRLF on a Windows checkout and the
# fingerprint gate fails. The sidecar is pinned for the same reason.
src/tenantless/profiles/demo.json text eol=lf
tests/demo_profile.sha256 text eol=lf

# Container build inputs MUST stay LF on every platform. A CRLF shebang or heredoc
# in the generator entrypoint breaks `docker build` — the COPY carries CRLF into the
# image and `#!/bin/sh\r` / the inlined `python - <<'PY'` heredoc fail at runtime.
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites these to CRLF on a Windows checkout without the pin.
docker/generator-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
generator.Dockerfile text eol=lf
generator.Dockerfile.dockerignore text eol=lf

# Release/E2E shell scripts run by `bash …` on the Linux CI runner — a CRLF shebang
# or heredoc breaks them. Pin LF so a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) cannot
# introduce CR into the committed blob.
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
